  "description": "This bike was built for pure fun whether you're a growing tween or a parent riding with your kiddo. The Axios 24 is a BMX race-inspired cruiser bike that's great for beginning rides at the bike park, pump track or reliving glory days at the BMX track with friends and fam (or cruising the neighborhood).\nLightweight 6061 aluminum BMX frame – great for teen and adult riders. 21.7\" top tube length fits riders 5'6\" or taller.\nDrivetrain features 175 mm one-piece Hi-Ten steel cranks with a 42T chainring and American loose ball bottom bracket.\n24” x 1.95” tires mounted on aluminum single wall 36H rims with aluminum ball bearer front hub and 18T cog freewheel ball bearing rear hub.\nHi-ten steel handlebar and fork, 50 mm stem, threadless 1-1/8\" external headset, and aluminum linear pull brakes and brake levers.",
